{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Confirmed RCA before Phase 2\n\n`close_precheck._completion_precheck` reads ticket state from the relocated tracker correctly, then wrongly derives the code repository as `os.path.dirname(tracker)`. `_referencing_commits` consequently runs `git -C <tracker-parent> log` instead of scanning the explicit/current code checkout. The same root conflation reaches completion-gate config because transition_compute also sets repo_root_str from the tracker parent.\n\nRuntime proof used disposable, separate code and tracker repositories: the correct code-root scan found the trailer commit while the tracker-parent scan returned none. CLI close either emitted the false missing-commit diagnostic when the external parent enabled the gate, or silently closed unsigned when that parent had no gate config. Changing only git -C distinguished the root cause from malformed trailers, resolver failure, reachability, and verifier failure. Default in-repo and true-missing controls remained correct.\n\nLegitimacy: defect. Absolute relocated trackers are documented/supported; the close contract grounds referencing commits in current worktree HEAD.\n\nApproved repair seam: use `config.repo_root(repo_root)` (explicit -> REBAR_ROOT -> cwd Git toplevel), which already resolves the default completion HEAD. Do not use LLM `resolve_code_root`, which may select an attested snapshot and would couple deterministic close logic to the LLM boundary. Normalize both code scan and completion-gate/autoresume config roots; fixing only git -C leaves silent gate bypass.\n\nCaller gate: CLI, library, MCP, and automated import all converge through transition_compute/shared close core; none relies on tracker-parent-as-code. Exact sibling candidate `commit_impact.code_root_for` repeats the tracker-parent assumption for attach-commits and requires separate debugging rather than silent inclusion."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787025631163949001,"uuid":"e5bf4613-190b-431c-8b92-ade8bed9f023"}